.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-36-## What it does
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-37-
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-38-- Reorders uniquely identifiable stable system-prompt content before dynamic context. If the same candidate appears more than once (for example, quoted inside dynamic context), it is left unchanged to avoid removing the wrong occurrence.
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-39-- Compresses Pi skill listings and strips session-overview churn.
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md:40:- Requests long cache retention when Pi/provider compat supports it.
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-41-- Adds a session-id `prompt_cache_key` fallback for `openai-completions` / `openai-responses` payloads when no effective key exists, including Pi's built-in `llama.cpp` provider as Pi 0.82+ core does.
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md:42:- Warns once for third-party OpenAI-compatible proxies missing cache/session-affinity compat flags.
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md:43:- Detects adaptive-thinking compat for Claude (opus-4.6+ including Opus 5, sonnet-4.6+ including Sonnet 5, fable-5+) and Kimi Coding K3 / `kimi-for-coding` custom channels.
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-44-- Shows daily cumulative provider/model footer stats by default, with an opt-in current-session display mode.
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-45-- Reports input cost, savings against a fully-uncached baseline, and prefix churn through `/cache-optimizer stats`, priced from the model registry rather than hardcoded rates.
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md:46:- Stops paid retry loops: tracks tool-call batches and escalates only when a whole batch fails repeatedly, with any successful call resetting the streaks.
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-47-- Supports optional router-extension integration through versioned global protocols (`Symbol.for("pi.routing.registry.v1")` and `Symbol.for("pi.cache.hints.v1")`) without importing router packages.
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-48-
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-49-Caching is provider-side and best-effort. Third-party proxies and router extensions can still hide cache usage, reject unsupported parameters, or route requests across multiple upstreams.
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-50-
--
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-70-
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-71-| Command | Effect |
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-72-|---|---|
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-73-| `/cache-optimizer` | Interactive menu when UI supports it; otherwise prints help and current state. |
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md:74:| `/cache-optimizer enable` | Enables runtime optimizations for the current Pi process, resets local footer stats, and starts a fresh “enabled” measurement. |
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md:75:| `/cache-optimizer disable` | Disables optimization for the current Pi process, resets local footer stats, and keeps collecting footer stats in disabled comparison mode. Run `/reload` or restart Pi to return to startup behavior. |
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md:76:| `/cache-optimizer doctor` | Shows active model/provider/API/base URL/compat plus low-hit diagnosis. |
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md:77:| `/cache-optimizer compat` | Shows copyable compat advice for the active model, if applicable. |
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-78-| `/cache-optimizer stats` | Shows today's local provider/model counters, recent trend, input cost, estimated savings against a fully-uncached baseline, and detected prefix churn for the active model. |
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md:79:| `/cache-optimizer reset` | Resets local footer stats for the active provider/model; upstream provider cache is not modified. |
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-80-| `/cache-optimizer config footer-mode total\|session\|process` | Persist the footer stats mode. Persistent command configuration overrides the environment variable. |
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md:81:| `/cache-optimizer fix` | Auto-repairs safe compat issues for the active model (adaptive thinking, DeepSeek reasoning, OpenAI proxy session affinity). Shows preview + risk warning, requires confirmation. **Only modifies `models.json` after explicit user approval.** |
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-82-
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-83-The interactive `/cache-optimizer` menu includes `Footer mode`, where you can choose `total`, `session`, or `process`. `enable` / `disable` are current-process switches. For a persistent opt-out, use environment variables below.
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-84-
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-85-## Persistent opt-out
--
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-87-| Env var | Effect |
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-88-|---|---|
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-89-| `PI_CACHE_OPTIMIZER_NO_PROMPT_REWRITE=1` | Disable prompt mutations only; footer stats and cache-key fallback remain active. |
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-90-| `PI_CACHE_OPTIMIZER_NO_SKILL_COMPRESSION=1` | Keep Pi's verbose skill XML. |
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md:91:| `PI_CACHE_OPTIMIZER_NO_OPENAI_CACHE_KEY=1` | Disable the OpenAI-compatible `prompt_cache_key` fallback. Preferred explicit opt-out. |
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-92-| `PI_CACHE_OPTIMIZER_OPENAI_CACHE_KEY=0` | Disable the same fallback via the legacy inverse switch. Values `0`, `false`, `no`, or `off` disable it. |
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-93-
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-94-## Retry loop guard
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-95-
--
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-99-
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-100-- The 3rd consecutive all-failed batch gets a `[loop guard]` notice appended to the tool result the model sees, telling it to change arguments, use another tool, or report the blocker. The turn is not ended.
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-101-- The 4th consecutive all-failed batch stops the turn: a notification is shown and the agent operation is aborted, so the same request is not billed again.
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-102-
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md:103:**What resets the streaks:**
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-104-
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-105-- Any successful tool call — a partial success means the turn is converging, not looping.
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-106-- The assistant moving on without calling any tools.
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-107-- A new session. Guard state is per-session, in-memory only, and never written to disk.
--
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-110-
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-111-- It never rewrites, retries, or "fixes" the user's request to make a call succeed.
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-112-- It cannot fire on a first attempt, and one legitimate retry never triggers it: escalation requires three consecutive all-failed batches.
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-113-- It does not change transport-level retry policy; provider-side retries remain the provider's concern.
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md:114:- It does not affect cache measurement, prompt rewriting, compat warnings, `doctor`, or `fix`.
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-115-
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-116-## Hash-verified edits
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-117-
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-118-Exact-string editing fails silently when a file changes between the model's read and its edit: the edit still matches somewhere and lands on the wrong lines. This extension adds a hash-anchored editing path that carries the evidence instead.
--
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-130-**v2.7.0+** supports daily cumulative and conversation-session footer scopes. **v2.7.1** adds the Footer mode option to the interactive `/cache-optimizer` menu. **v2.8.0+** also supports process-scoped counters. The footer defaults to `total`, which shows the provider/model's local counters for the current day across Pi sessions and process restarts. Use either the command or environment variable to select the scope:
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-131-
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-132-| Value | Effect |
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-133-|---|---|
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md:134:| `total` (default) | Show today's restart-persistent provider/model totals across sessions. Local day rollover resets the counters. |
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-135-| `session` | Show only the current hashed Pi conversation session's counters. A fresh conversation session starts at `0/0`; restarting Pi while resuming the same session restores that session bucket. |
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-136-
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-137-| `process` | Show only counters collected by the current Pi process. It starts at `0/0` after Pi restart or extension reload and is never restored from disk. |
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-138-
--
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-145-```
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-146-
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-147-The explicit setting is stored in `pi-cache-optimizer-config.json` under Pi's agent directory. If no command override exists, `PI_CACHE_OPTIMIZER_FOOTER_MODE=total|session|process` is used; values are case-insensitive, and missing or invalid values fall back to `total`. To return an existing installation to environment-controlled behavior, manually delete `pi-cache-optimizer-config.json` and run `/reload`.
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-148-
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md:149:## OpenAI-compatible proxy setup
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-150-
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-151-Third-party `openai-completions` proxies (LiteLLM / OneAPI / NewAPI / OpenRouter-like channels) often route one session across multiple upstream backends. That splits provider-side prompt caches.
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-152-
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md:153:Pi 0.81+ also has a built-in `llama.cpp` provider using an OpenAI-shaped transport. Pi 0.82+ core generates a session `prompt_cache_key` for it when cache retention is enabled, so this extension preserves that key and may add the same conservative fallback when missing. The built-in provider's explicit compat fingerprint is excluded from generic proxy routing/session-affinity advice, but a custom or overridden provider that merely reuses the id `llama.cpp` is treated like any other OpenAI-compatible channel. `prompt_cache_retention` remains subject to the normal safety rule: keep it only for official OpenAI or an explicit effective `supportsLongCacheRetention: true` opt-in in `models.json`; otherwise strip it before sending. Effective values follow Pi's precedence: `modelOverrides[modelId].compat` first, then the matching `models[].compat`, then provider-level `compat`. An explicit `false` at a higher layer overrides `true` below it.
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-154-
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-155-For real proxies, start with session affinity:
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-156-
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-157-```json
--
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-160-    "your-provider-id": {
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-161-      "api": "openai-completions",
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-162-      "baseUrl": "https://example.com/v1",
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-163-      "apiKey": "env:YOUR_API_KEY",
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md:164:      "compat": {
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-165-        "sendSessionAffinityHeaders": true
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-166-      },
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-167-      "models": [
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-168-        { "id": "gpt-5.5", "name": "GPT-5.5" }
--
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-176-
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-177-- `sendSessionAffinityHeaders: true` is the safe default when your proxy supports sticky routing.
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-178-- `supportsLongCacheRetention: true` is optional. Add it only when the endpoint explicitly supports OpenAI long prompt cache retention.
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-179-- If you see `400 Unsupported parameter: prompt_cache_retention`, remove/avoid `supportsLongCacheRetention` for that channel. Keep `sendSessionAffinityHeaders` if supported.
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md:180:- Use `/cache-optimizer compat` or `/cache-optimizer doctor` to see model-specific advice.
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md:181:- For DeepSeek models, the Pi Mono guidance expects `compat.requiresReasoningContentOnAssistantMessages: true` and `compat.thinkingFormat: "deepseek"` alongside cache/session-affinity flags when the endpoint supports them.
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md:182:- This extension's `doctor` and `compat` commands only advise; they do not modify `models.json`.
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-183-
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md:184:## Anthropic cache TTL compatibility
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-185-
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-186-Anthropic processes cache breakpoints in `tools → system → messages` order and rejects a `ttl: "1h"` breakpoint that appears after a 5-minute breakpoint. An ephemeral `cache_control` without `ttl` uses the default 5-minute retention.
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-187-
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-188-For every `anthropic-messages` channel, the extension checks the final serialized payload and immediately downgrades a visibly invalid short-to-long transition. Legal long-only and `1h → 5m` payloads remain unchanged, including third-party endpoints that genuinely support 1-hour retention.
--
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-190-Some proxies rewrite or insert hidden 5-minute breakpoints after Pi's request hook. If a provider returns Anthropic's explicit TTL-ordering error, the extension records a process-local provider/model fallback so the next subsequent request uses the default 5-minute TTL. This error is a non-retryable HTTP 400 in Pi 0.82.1, so the extension does not claim that Pi's automatic retry will rerun the failed turn; if another layer retries it, that retry also uses the fallback. `/cache-optimizer doctor` reports the fallback and `/cache-optimizer fix` can persist a model-scoped `supportsLongCacheRetention: false` with the normal confirmation/backup flow. Other 400 errors and prompt-too-long failures do not activate this fallback. The runtime observation lasts until the current process exits and survives extension reloads within that process.
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-191-
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-192-## Adaptive thinking models
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-193-
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md:194:Claude models from opus-4.6 / sonnet-4.6 (including Opus 5 and Sonnet 5) / fable-5 onwards require `forceAdaptiveThinking: true` in compat. Kimi Coding K3 (`k3`) and `kimi-for-coding` also use adaptive thinking and need `allowEmptySignature: true` so replayed empty-signature thinking blocks remain valid. Without the required compat, Pi may send a legacy thinking payload or replay thinking incorrectly. Pi 0.83.0's native Opus 5 catalog is covered by the same adaptive-thinking detection; custom `anthropic-messages` channels still need the compat flag when Pi does not provide it.
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-195-
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-196-Pi's built-in catalog already sets this flag for official models. Custom channels in `models.json` that override these models must include the flag:
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-197-
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-198-```json
--
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-201-    "your-claude-channel": {
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-202-      "api": "anthropic-messages",
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-203-      "baseUrl": "https://...",
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-204-      "apiKey": "env:YOUR_KEY",
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md:205:      "compat": {
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-206-        "forceAdaptiveThinking": true
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-207-      },
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-208-      "models": [
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-209-        { "id": "claude-sonnet-5", "name": "Claude Sonnet 5" }
--
