.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-256-
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-257-## Auto-repair with `/cache-optimizer fix`
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-258-
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md:259:**v2.6.0+** adds a `fix` subcommand that can auto-repair safe compat issues:
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-260-
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-261-- Adaptive thinking (`forceAdaptiveThinking: true`; Kimi Coding K3 / `kimi-for-coding` also `allowEmptySignature: true`)
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md:262:- DeepSeek Pi Mono reasoning compat (`thinkingFormat: "deepseek"`, `requiresReasoningContentOnAssistantMessages: true`)
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md:263:- OpenAI-compatible proxy session affinity (`sendSessionAffinityHeaders: true` for `openai-completions`). Pi 0.80.7+ controls `openai-responses` header shape with `sessionAffinityFormat` and auto-detects its default; this extension no longer writes the removed `sendSessionIdHeader` field.
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-264-
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-265-**Scope:** only the currently active model. Other channels require switching models and running `fix` again.
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-266-
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-267-**Safety:**
--
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-272-4. Requires explicit user confirmation (interactive prompt or `ui.select`)
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-273-5. Writes atomically (temp + rename); self-validates after write
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-274-6. Falls back to manual guidance if JSONC scanner cannot confidently locate the target
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-275-
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md:276:Existing `modelOverrides[modelId]` entries have Pi's highest precedence, so `fix` repairs them directly. For built-in or API-login models without a custom `models[]` entry, `fix` creates a compat-only `modelOverrides` entry instead of inventing a custom model definition. Self-validation checks the effective three-layer compat result, so a lower-level edit shadowed by an override is rejected.
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-277-
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-278-**Non-interactive mode:** refuses to write; shows manual edit guidance instead.
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-279-
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md:280:**Run:** `/cache-optimizer fix` when the active model has detected compat issues. The command shows "nothing to fix" when compat is already complete.
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-281-
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-282-### Channels without a `models.json` provider entry
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-283-
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md:284:Some Pi channels may be available even when there is no provider block in Pi's agent `models.json` yet (default: `~/.pi/agent/models.json`; with `PI_CODING_AGENT_DIR`, use `$PI_CODING_AGENT_DIR/models.json`). Keep existing authentication as-is and do not copy credentials, tokens, or API keys. Add only cache/routing compatibility overrides in `models.json`.
