.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-367-
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md:368:`message_end` treats these assistant-message fields as authoritative. If `provider` + `model`/`responseModel` + cache usage are present, stats update the upstream bucket even when the active model is still `router/auto`. If upstream usage does not expose cache fields, leave them absent/zero; this extension will not fake cache hits.
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-369-
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-370-### Optional: live route registry for pre-response UX
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-371-
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md:372:Final message metadata is enough for post-response stats. For pre-response flows — footer display before the first response, `/cache-optimizer doctor`, `/cache-optimizer compat`, `/cache-optimizer reset`, and OpenAI-compatible `prompt_cache_key` fallback — register a live route adapter under `Symbol.for("pi.routing.registry.v1")`.
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-373-
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-374-Protocol shape:
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-375-
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-376-```ts
