specs/hooks/019-cache-optimizer-measurement-fixes/plan.md-47-## 2. APPROACH
specs/hooks/019-cache-optimizer-measurement-fixes/plan.md-48-
specs/hooks/019-cache-optimizer-measurement-fixes/plan.md-49-**W1 first, because it defines the vocabulary.** Classification moves to field presence rather than
specs/hooks/019-cache-optimizer-measurement-fixes/plan.md-50-value, so an absent signal is distinguishable from a measured zero. Two counters on one code path:
specs/hooks/019-cache-optimizer-measurement-fixes/plan.md-51-cost and token totals always record; only the hit ratio's numerator and denominator exclude an
specs/hooks/019-cache-optimizer-measurement-fixes/plan.md:52:unreported sample. A new `unmeasuredRequests` counter makes the exclusion visible instead of silent,
specs/hooks/019-cache-optimizer-measurement-fixes/plan.md-53-and `totalRequests` keeps its current meaning so no existing reader shifts under it.
specs/hooks/019-cache-optimizer-measurement-fixes/plan.md-54-
specs/hooks/019-cache-optimizer-measurement-fixes/plan.md-55-**W2 is one predicate.** `<= 0` becomes a missing-or-negative test, so an authoritative zero prices
specs/hooks/019-cache-optimizer-measurement-fixes/plan.md-56-as free. The cost arithmetic already handles a zero rate.
specs/hooks/019-cache-optimizer-measurement-fixes/plan.md-57-
specs/hooks/019-cache-optimizer-measurement-fixes/plan.md:58:**W3 is one flag.** `reportsCacheUsage` on `CacheCompat`. It is not a substitute for W1 and is not
specs/hooks/019-cache-optimizer-measurement-fixes/plan.md-59-merged into it: W1 handles the per-response case, W3 covers the case where the host synthesizes
specs/hooks/019-cache-optimizer-measurement-fixes/plan.md-60-zeros before the extension can see anything.
specs/hooks/019-cache-optimizer-measurement-fixes/plan.md-61-
specs/hooks/019-cache-optimizer-measurement-fixes/plan.md-62-**W4 gates prefix lifting on cross-turn stability**, keeping authorization state separate from churn
specs/hooks/019-cache-optimizer-measurement-fixes/plan.md-63-state. It lands after W1 so its effect on hit rate is measurable rather than asserted.
--
