.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-35-
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-36-## What it does
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-37-
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-38-- Reorders uniquely identifiable stable system-prompt content before dynamic context. If the same candidate appears more than once (for example, quoted inside dynamic context), it is left unchanged to avoid removing the wrong occurrence.
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-39-- Compresses Pi skill listings and strips session-overview churn.
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-40-- Requests long cache retention when Pi/provider compat supports it.
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-41-- Adds a session-id `prompt_cache_key` fallback for `openai-completions` / `openai-responses` payloads when no effective key exists, including Pi's built-in `llama.cpp` provider as Pi 0.82+ core does.
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-42-- Warns once for third-party OpenAI-compatible proxies missing cache/session-affinity compat flags.
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-43-- Detects adaptive-thinking compat for Claude (opus-4.6+ including Opus 5, sonnet-4.6+ including Sonnet 5, fable-5+) and Kimi Coding K3 / `kimi-for-coding` custom channels.
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-44-- Shows daily cumulative provider/model footer stats by default, with an opt-in current-session display mode.
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-45-- Reports input cost, savings against a fully-uncached baseline, and prefix churn through `/cache-optimizer stats`, priced from the model registry rather than hardcoded rates.
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-46-- Stops paid retry loops: tracks tool-call batches and escalates only when a whole batch fails repeatedly, with any successful call resetting the streaks.
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md:47:- Supports optional router-extension integration through versioned global protocols (`Symbol.for("pi.routing.registry.v1")` and `Symbol.for("pi.cache.hints.v1")`) without importing router packages.
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-48-
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md:49:Caching is provider-side and best-effort. Third-party proxies and router extensions can still hide cache usage, reject unsupported parameters, or route requests across multiple upstreams.
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-50-
