.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-146-
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-147-The explicit setting is stored in `pi-cache-optimizer-config.json` under Pi's agent directory. If no command override exists, `PI_CACHE_OPTIMIZER_FOOTER_MODE=total|session|process` is used; values are case-insensitive, and missing or invalid values fall back to `total`. To return an existing installation to environment-controlled behavior, manually delete `pi-cache-optimizer-config.json` and run `/reload`.
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-148-
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-149-## OpenAI-compatible proxy setup
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-150-
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md:151:Third-party `openai-completions` proxies (LiteLLM / OneAPI / NewAPI / OpenRouter-like channels) often route one session across multiple upstream backends. That splits provider-side prompt caches.
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-152-
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-153-Pi 0.81+ also has a built-in `llama.cpp` provider using an OpenAI-shaped transport. Pi 0.82+ core generates a session `prompt_cache_key` for it when cache retention is enabled, so this extension preserves that key and may add the same conservative fallback when missing. The built-in provider's explicit compat fingerprint is excluded from generic proxy routing/session-affinity advice, but a custom or overridden provider that merely reuses the id `llama.cpp` is treated like any other OpenAI-compatible channel. `prompt_cache_retention` remains subject to the normal safety rule: keep it only for official OpenAI or an explicit effective `supportsLongCacheRetention: true` opt-in in `models.json`; otherwise strip it before sending. Effective values follow Pi's precedence: `modelOverrides[modelId].compat` first, then the matching `models[].compat`, then provider-level `compat`. An explicit `false` at a higher layer overrides `true` below it.
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-154-
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-155-For real proxies, start with session affinity:
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-156-
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-157-```json
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-158-{
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-159-  "providers": {
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-160-    "your-provider-id": {
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-161-      "api": "openai-completions",
--
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-169-      ]
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-170-    }
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-171-  }
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-172-}
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-173-```
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-174-
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-175-Notes:
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-176-
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-177-- `sendSessionAffinityHeaders: true` is the safe default when your proxy supports sticky routing.
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-178-- `supportsLongCacheRetention: true` is optional. Add it only when the endpoint explicitly supports OpenAI long prompt cache retention.
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md:179:- `reportsCacheUsage` tells the extension whether the provider reports cache-usage fields. When unset, the extension follows the response's cache fields. With `false`, requests are routed to unmeasured rather than counted as misses.
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-180-- If you see `400 Unsupported parameter: prompt_cache_retention`, remove/avoid `supportsLongCacheRetention` for that channel. Keep `sendSessionAffinityHeaders` if supported.
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-181-- Use `/cache-optimizer compat` or `/cache-optimizer doctor` to see model-specific advice.
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-182-- For DeepSeek models, the Pi Mono guidance expects `compat.requiresReasoningContentOnAssistantMessages: true` and `compat.thinkingFormat: "deepseek"` alongside cache/session-affinity flags when the endpoint supports them.
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-183-- This extension's `doctor` and `compat` commands only advise; they do not modify `models.json`.
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-184-
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-185-## Anthropic cache TTL compatibility
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-186-
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-187-Anthropic processes cache breakpoints in `tools → system → messages` order and rejects a `ttl: "1h"` breakpoint that appears after a 5-minute breakpoint. An ephemeral `cache_control` without `ttl` uses the default 5-minute retention.
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-188-
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-189-For every `anthropic-messages` channel, the extension checks the final serialized payload and immediately downgrades a visibly invalid short-to-long transition. Legal long-only and `1h → 5m` payloads remain unchanged, including third-party endpoints that genuinely support 1-hour retention.
--
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-337-```text
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-338-OpenAI cache 3/10 · 0.002M/0.005M tok (40%) ⚠️ compat
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-339-```
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-340-
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-341-Format: `<label> <hit requests>/<total requests> · <cached input tokens>/<total input tokens> tok (<token hit rate>)`. Some adapters may also append `· write <tokens> tok`, and runtime diagnostics may append `⚠️ compat` or `⚠️ integrity`.
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-342-
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-343-Supported footer labels include: DS, Claude, OpenAI, Gemini, Kimi, Qwen, GLM, MiniMax, Mimo, Hunyuan, Mistral, Grok, Llama, Nemotron, Cohere, Yi, Doubao, ERNIE, Baichuan, StepFun, Spark, InternLM, Gemma, Phi, Jamba, Solar, Sonar, Nova, Reka, Falcon, DBRX, MPT, StableLM, Aquila, EXAONE, HyperCLOVA, Luminous, Hermes, Granite, Arctic, Pangu, SenseNova, Zhinao, MiniCPM, XVERSE, Orion, OpenChat, Vicuna, Wizard, Zephyr, Dolphin, OpenOrca, Starling, BLOOM, RWKV, and Aya.
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-344-
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-345-Adapter selection uses only model id/name (plus assistant message model/name on message end). Generic OpenAI-shaped APIs are not treated as OpenAI-family unless the model id/name matches a supported family.
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-346-
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md:347:## For router / virtual-channel extension authors
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-348-
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md:349:If your Pi extension provides a virtual routing provider (for example `router/auto`, `router/smart`, or a profile/channel that forwards to a real upstream), this extension can show cache stats for the real upstream provider/model instead of the virtual shell. Integration is optional, versioned, and does **not** require importing this package.
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-350-
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-351-### Minimum integration: final assistant message metadata
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-352-
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-353-For seamless final cache-stat attribution, relay the real upstream identity on completed assistant messages:
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-354-
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-355-```ts
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-356-{
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-357-  role: "assistant",
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-358-  provider: "anthropic",              // real upstream provider
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-359-  responseModel: "claude-opus-4-8",   // or model: "..."
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-360-  api: "anthropic-messages",          // upstream Pi API id when known
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-361-  usage: {
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-362-    input: 1200,       // Pi-normalized uncached input tokens, if available
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-363-    cacheRead: 8000,   // tokens read from provider prompt cache
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-364-    cacheWrite: 500,   // tokens newly written to provider prompt cache
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-365-  },
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-366-}
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-367-```
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-368-
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md:369:`message_end` treats these assistant-message fields as authoritative. If `provider` + `model`/`responseModel` + cache usage are present, stats update the upstream bucket even when the active model is still `router/auto`. If upstream usage does not expose cache fields, leave them absent/zero; this extension will not fake cache hits.
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-370-
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md:371:### Optional: live route registry for pre-response UX
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-372-
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md:373:Final message metadata is enough for post-response stats. For pre-response flows — footer display before the first response, `/cache-optimizer doctor`, `/cache-optimizer compat`, `/cache-optimizer reset`, and OpenAI-compatible `prompt_cache_key` fallback — register a live route adapter under `Symbol.for("pi.routing.registry.v1")`.
