.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-444-
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md:445:When the query matches the current session/route, `hints` may contain `systemPrompt`, `promptCacheKey`, and `cacheRetention: "long"`. Treat these as advisory and sensitive: do not log them, do not expose prompt text, and do not overwrite an existing request-level `prompt_cache_key` / `promptCacheKey`.
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-446-
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-447-### Security and correctness rules
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-448-
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-449-- Do not import `pi-cache-optimizer`; use `Symbol.for(...)` discovery only.
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md:450:- Do not expose API keys, prompts, payloads, headers, response bodies, or model output in route snapshots or logs.
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-451-- Use assistant-message metadata for final attribution; live registry data is advisory and may be stale by response time.
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-452-- Preserve truthful usage. Missing cache usage should show as 0/under-reported, not as synthetic hits.
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-453-
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/README.md-454-## Uninstall
